  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  build_number: 0\n  name: sbcl\n  version: \"2.6.8\"\n  sh: ${{ \".sh\" if unix else \".bat\" }}\n\npackage:\n  name: sbcl\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  - url: http://prdownloads.sourceforge.net/sbcl/sbcl-${{ version }}-source.tar.bz2\n    sha256: ad5126dfdfba5db27ee77bcc25893020fe522d0b7653d45b4c4795ade3ddc23d\n    target_directory: sbcl-source\n    patches:\n      - if: linux\n        then:\n          - patches/linux/0001-x86_64-aarch64-ppc64le-zstd.patch\n          - patches/linux/0002-target-runtime-launcher.patch\n      - if: target_platform == \"linux-riscv64\"\n        then:\n          - patches/linux/0003-target-runtime-launcher-contrib.patch\n      - if: osx\n        then:\n          - patches/osx/0001-update-rpath-zstd.patch\n      - if: not unix\n        then:\n          - patches/win/0001-rewrite-long-xargs.patch\n          - patches/win/0002-add-link-zstd.patch\n          - patches/win/0003-add-build-dll.patch\n          - patches/win/0004-improve-sbcl_home-test.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: ${{ build_number }}\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - if: unix\n      then:\n        - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n      else:\n        - ${{ compiler('m2w64_c') }}\n        - m2-coreutils\n        - m2-findutils\n        - m2-grep\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - make\n    - if: riscv64 or ppc64le\n      then:\n        - qemu-execve-${{ target_platform | replace(\"linux-\", \"\") }}\n    - sbcl\n  host:\n    # zstd not yet available\n    - if: not (osx and arm64) and not riscv64\n      then:\n        - zstd\n\ntests:\n  - package_contents:\n      strict: true\n      bin:\n        - sbcl\n      lib:\n        - if: unix\n          then:\n            - sbcl\n      files:\n        - etc/conda/activate.d/sbcl-activate${{ sh }}\n        - etc/conda/deactivate.d/sbcl-deactivate${{ sh }}\n        - if: osx\n          then:\n            - lib/libsbcl.so\n        - if: not unix\n          then:\n            - bin/libsbcl.dll\n            - lib/libsbcl.lib\n        - lib/sbcl/contrib/{asdf,uiop}.fasl\n        - lib/sbcl/contrib/sb-{aclrepl,bsd-sockets,capstone,cltl2,concurrency,cover}.{asd,fasl}\n        - lib/sbcl/contrib/sb-{executable,gmp,grovel,introspect,manual,md5,mpfr}.{asd,fasl}\n        - lib/sbcl/contrib/sb-{posix,queue,rotate-byte,rt,simd,simple-streams,sprof}.{asd,fasl}\n        - lib/sbcl/sbcl.core\n        - lib/sbcl/sbcl.mk\n        - share/doc/sbcl/{BUGS,COPYING,CREDITS,NEWS}\n        - share/man/man1/sbcl.1\n        - if: linux\n          then:\n            - lib/sbcl/contrib/sb-perf.{asd,fasl}\n        - if: x86_64\n          then:\n            - lib/sbcl/contrib/sb-simd.{asd,fasl}\n\n  - script:\n      - sbcl --version\n      - sbcl --help\n      - sbcl --noinform --disable-debugger --eval \"(print (require :asdf))\" --disable-debugger --eval \"(quit)\"\n    requirements:\n      run:\n        - if: linux and not (target_platform == \"linux-ppc64le\" or target_platform == \"linux-riscv64\")\n          then:\n            - strace\n\nabout:\n  homepage: http://www.sbcl.org\n  license: BSD-2-Clause AND MIT\n  summary: Steel Bank Common Lisp (SBCL) is a high performance Common Lisp compiler\n  description: |\n    Steel Bank Common Lisp (SBCL) is a high performance Common Lisp compiler.\n    It is open source / free software, with a permissive license. In addition to the\n    compiler and runtime system for ANSI Common Lisp, it provides an interactive\n    environment including a debugger, a statistical profiler, a code coverage tool,\n    and many other extensions.\n  documentation: http://www.sbcl.org/manual/index.html\n  license_file:\n    - COPYING\n    - CREDITS\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - MementoRC\n    - wolfv\n    - Tobias-Fischer\n",
